---
import trustpointLogo from "../img/trustpoint_labs_logo.svg?url";
import trustpointFavicon from "../img/trustpoint_favicon.png?url";

import "@fontsource/open-sauce-one/400.css";
import "@fontsource/open-sauce-one/500.css";
import "@fontsource/open-sauce-one/600.css";
import "@fontsource/open-sauce-one/700.css";

import "../styles/global.css";

const githubUrl = "https://github.com/Trustpoint-Project";
---

<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />

    <meta
      name="viewport"
      content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"
    />

    <meta
      name="description"
      content="Privacy policy for the Trustpoint Labs website."
    />

    <title>Privacy | Trustpoint Labs</title>

    <link
      rel="icon"
      type="image/png"
      href={trustpointFavicon}
    />
  </head>

  <body>

    <header class="shell">

      <a
        class="logo-link"
        href="/"
        aria-label="Trustpoint Labs"
      >
        <img
          class="logo"
          src={trustpointLogo}
          alt="Trustpoint Labs"
        />
      </a>

      <nav aria-label="Main navigation">
        <a href="/">Home</a>

        <a
          class="github"
          href={githubUrl}
          target="_blank"
          rel="noreferrer"
        >
          GitHub
          <span>↗︎</span>
        </a>
      </nav>

    </header>


    <main>

      <section class="legal-page shell">

        <div class="section-label">
          <span class="square"></span>
          PRIVACY
        </div>

        <h1 class="legal-title">
          Privacy Policy
        </h1>

        <p class="legal-intro">
          This privacy policy explains how personal data is processed
          when you visit the Trustpoint Labs website or contact us
          through the website.
        </p>


        <div class="legal-content">

          <section>
            <h2>1. Controller</h2>

            <p>
              The controller within the meaning of the General Data
              Protection Regulation (GDPR) is:
            </p>

            <p>
              Campus Schwarzwald gGmbH<br />
              Herzog-Eberhard-Straße 56<br />
              72250 Freudenstadt<br />
              Germany
            </p>

            <p>
              Phone:
              <a href="tel:+4974418684900">
                +49 7441 868490-0
              </a>
              <br />

              Email:
              <a href="mailto:info@campus-schwarzwald.de">
                info@campus-schwarzwald.de
              </a>
            </p>

            <p>
              Trustpoint Labs is currently an initiative of
              Campus Schwarzwald gGmbH and is not yet a separate
              legal entity.
            </p>
          </section>


          <section>
            <h2>2. Hosting</h2>

            <p>
              This website is hosted using services provided by
              Netlify, Inc., 101 2nd Street, San Francisco,
              California 94105, USA.
            </p>

            <p>
              When you access this website, technical information may
              be processed in order to deliver the website securely and
              reliably. This may include, for example, your IP address,
              date and time of access, requested resource, browser type,
              operating system and technical request information.
            </p>

            <p>
              Processing is based on Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR. Our legitimate
              interest is the secure, reliable and efficient provision
              of this website.
            </p>

            <p>
              Netlify may process data outside the European Economic
              Area. According to Netlify, international transfers are
              safeguarded through appropriate mechanisms including
              the EU Standard Contractual Clauses and, where applicable,
              the EU-U.S. Data Privacy Framework.
            </p>
          </section>


          <section>
            <h2>3. Contact form</h2>

            <p>
              If you contact us using the contact form, we process the
              information you provide in order to respond to your
              inquiry.
            </p>

            <p>
              Depending on the information you submit, this may include:
            </p>

            <ul>
              <li>Name</li>
              <li>Work email address</li>
              <li>Company or organisation</li>
              <li>Your message or project requirements</li>
              <li>Number of devices, if provided</li>
              <li>Deployment environment, if provided</li>
            </ul>

            <p>
              Where your inquiry relates to a potential contractual
              relationship, processing is based on Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR.
              For other inquiries, processing is based on our legitimate
              interest in responding to business and technical requests
              pursuant to Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR.
            </p>

            <p>
              Form submissions are processed using Netlify Forms.
              The submitted information is therefore transmitted to
              and processed by Netlify on our behalf.
            </p>

            <p>
              We retain inquiry data only for as long as necessary to
              process the inquiry and any resulting business relationship,
              unless statutory retention obligations require a longer
              retention period.
            </p>
          </section>


          <section>
            <h2>4. Contact by email</h2>

            <p>
              If you contact us by email, the information contained in
              your message is processed for the purpose of handling and
              responding to your inquiry.
            </p>

            <p>
              The legal basis is Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR where communication
              relates to a contract or pre-contractual measures, and
              otherwise Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR based on our legitimate
              interest in responding to inquiries.
            </p>
          </section>


          <section>
            <h2>5. Fonts</h2>

            <p>
              This website uses the Open Sauce One typeface.
              The font files are bundled with and served directly by
              this website. No connection to an external font provider
              is required when displaying the font.
            </p>
          </section>


          <section>
            <h2>6. GitHub and external links</h2>

            <p>
              This website contains links to external services,
              including GitHub. No personal data is transmitted to
              these services merely because a link is displayed.
            </p>

            <p>
              If you follow an external link, the privacy policy of the
              respective service applies.
            </p>
          </section>


          <section>
            <h2>7. Cookies and analytics</h2>

            <p>
              This website currently does not use analytics,
              advertising or tracking services and does not set
              non-essential cookies.
            </p>

            <p>
              If additional services requiring consent are introduced
              in the future, this privacy policy and the website's
              consent mechanism will be updated accordingly.
            </p>
          </section>


          <section>
            <h2>8. Your rights</h2>

            <p>
              Subject to the applicable legal requirements, you have
              the following rights regarding your personal data:
            </p>

            <ul>
              <li>Right of access under Art. 15 GDPR</li>
              <li>Right to rectification under Art. 16 GDPR</li>
              <li>Right to erasure under Art. 17 GDPR</li>
              <li>Right to restriction of processing under Art. 18 GDPR</li>
              <li>Right to data portability under Art. 20 GDPR</li>
              <li>Right to object under Art. 21 GDPR</li>
            </ul>

            <p>
              Where processing is based on consent, you may withdraw
              that consent at any time with effect for the future.
            </p>
          </section>


          <section>
            <h2>9. Right to lodge a complaint</h2>

            <p>
              You also have the right to lodge a complaint with a
              competent data protection supervisory authority if you
              believe that the processing of your personal data
              infringes applicable data protection law.
            </p>
          </section>


          <section>
            <h2>10. Security</h2>

            <p>
              We use appropriate technical and organisational measures
              to protect personal data against loss, misuse,
              unauthorised access and disclosure.
            </p>

            <p>
              The website is provided via encrypted HTTPS connections.
            </p>
          </section>


          <section>
            <h2>11. Changes to this privacy policy</h2>

            <p>
              We may update this privacy policy where the website,
              services or legal requirements change.
            </p>

            <p>
              Last updated: September 2026
            </p>
          </section>

        </div>

      </section>

    </main>


    <footer>

      <div class="footer-inner shell">

        <a
          href="/"
          aria-label="Trustpoint Labs"
        >
          <img
            class="footer-logo"
            src={trustpointLogo}
            alt="Trustpoint Labs"
          />
        </a>

        <div class="footer-links">
          <a href="/">Home</a>
          <a href="/imprint">Imprint</a>
          <a href="/privacy">Privacy</a>
        </div>

      </div>

    </footer>

  </body>
</html>